TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS ON PHASE-ATLAS LENSES
  leaders={ direct_p0: (0, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17), actual_residual: (0, 5, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17), pair_tax_shadow: (0, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 17, 18), eisenstein_norm: (0, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17) }
  score_hist={3: 1, 0: 1, 2: 1, 1: 1} directed_3cycles=0
  Hamiltonian_path=direct_p0 > pair_tax_shadow > eisenstein_norm > actual_residual
  challenged assumption: the natural vertices are not far runners; they are phase/support proof lenses and packet signatures.

SYNTHESIS
  Holding the rank-one relation u-2v+w=0 fixed does not freeze the packet signs.
  The mod-7 far phase and A2/Eisenstein chamber move large mass between actual residual,
  pair-tax shadow, and direct p0.  This explains why S51 saw AP-relation sign flips
  under shifts and why S52's cube-root coordinate is useful but not a proof scalar.
  Proof target: a finite resonant phase/support atlas for low-height relation tuples,
  followed by signed Abel/Koksma bounds only after the atlas key has been retained.
  No LRC(14) proof is claimed.
